    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily into speed and favorable matchups today, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) serving as our primary engine. His matchup against Lowder provides the perfect environment for his elite sprint speed to manifest into SB production, bolstered by Lowder\u2019s notoriously slow delivery to home, which adds 4% to our efficiency model. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.02) anchor the heart of the order with high-end projections. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start due to his elite 0.443 xwOBA, which survives the slight negative impact of his L/L platoon against P\u00e9rez, while **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a strong park factor and a favorable platoon advantage to maximize his scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Carson Benge** (33.04), who narrowly missed the cut. While his underlying metrics are solid, he was relegated to the pine due to a brutal combination of a tough matchup against S\u00e1nchez (2.95 xERA) and an unfavorable same-handed platoon disadvantage that pushed his efficiency well below our 40.0 floor. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.03) and **Josh Smith** (43.18); both sit near our threshold and face the formidable deGrom. While their scores are lower than typical starters, their roles in the lineup grant them just enough projected value to retain their spots. The Zebras' roster remains intact otherwise, with **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, and **Gary Sanchez** unavailable due to lineup adjustments, leaving us to rely on **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth** to provide necessary utility stability in the middle infield.",
